think The prior lap in this run landed color_swatch.rye's readable_scale (each tone paired with pure black or white by readable_ink). REMEMBER named the next agent-doable direction: a swatch scale keyed off best_ink over a keeper's own brand pair rather than pure black/white. That is the natural completion of the on-colour token -- a real design system inks against a brand's own light and dark text colours, not just the extremes.
think Additive and single-stranded on the same module: branded_swatch_at/branded_scale set each swatch's ink to color.best_ink(fill, ink_light, ink_dark) -- the higher-contrast of the keeper's two brand inks. color_scale still decides each fill, color still decides each ink; this only widens which two inks the pick chooses between.
think The crux proof is an SLC completeness argument: branded_scale is the GENERAL form and readable_scale the SPECIAL case. Because best_ink and readable_ink both break a tie toward the first/lighter ink, branded_scale(seed, white, black, dst) recovers readable_scale(seed, dst) byte-for-byte. The general verb contains the special one -- proven on metal, not claimed. Plus: a real navy/cream brand pair inks the same ramp, each ink exactly best_ink of its fill and always one of the two (never an invented third), and determinism across the brand variant.
obs GREEN on the metal re-run, no reds. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, >= 2 positive asserts per fn (the `or` membership checks live in `if` conditions, never in an assert, so no compound-assert ban is touched). The witness gained one native `contains` assertion for the reduction claim, honouring the REDS #76 loom; every elder assertion kept whole.
think Rota lap 16 read context/SIMPLE_LOVABLE_COMPLETE.md -- ship the smallest thing that is WHOLE, complete at its scope and lovable in use, claiming only what the work makes true. The reduction proof is exactly that spirit: the branded verb is complete because it demonstrably contains the readable one, nothing half-built.
